BLOCKER {"where": "Dependencies table, Horror Entities row (L439) and the Bidirectional summary row (L975)", "issue": "Both rows still give the Horror interface as the events DERELICT_LOADED / DERELICT_UNLOADED and POD_DEPARTED. The fixer rewrote the Attention row (L431), but these rows were missed. WM-31 and the POD_DEPARTED and DERELICT_LOADED/UNLOADED event rows now say Horror does not subscribe and reads web.view (pod_at, transit_state, leg_dir, leg_origin_id, leg_target_id, nodes[].loaded) in its hook. An implementer of Horror would read two contradictory interface contracts for the very fix blocker 1 was about.", "fix": "Rewrite both rows the way the Attention row now reads: Horror gets ring_of(section) plus the web.view reads named in WM-31, 'in place of the events', with the events kept only as the Audio notifications. Keep the HOR:369 quote and the confirmation text."}
NOTDONE [{"blocker": "ADR-0004 (the Alternative 9 rejection text) writes the counters as 'web.view.pod_arrived_seq', and its Web Map rows say 'web.state counters'. ADR-0006 1.12 and OQ-K say 'web.state read-view members'. This GDD puts them on the separate read web.save_seq(), not on web.view.", "reason": "ADRs are outside my edit scope and the ruling is that ADRs win. The ADR wording is loose about which read surface carries the counters, and the Web Map ADR (OQ-K) is where it gets fixed. If the ADR needs them literally on web.view, WM-36 and AC-WM-60 must be extended and the Chart Table GDD's web.view field-list assertion revisited. I kept web.view unchanged so the Chart Table contract is untouched."}]
REQ [{"registry": "design/registry/entities.yaml (web_events entry)", "entry": "web_events / web.state read surfaces", "change": "If the registry lists the web.state read members, add web.save_seq() -> {pod_arrived_seq, pod_arrived_seq u32, berthed_seq u32}, Save/Load facet only, non-persisted and non-hashed, alongside web.leg_timing(). Record that Attention and Horror read web.view members (pod_at, transit_state, leg_dir, leg_origin_id, leg_target_id, nodes[].loaded) instead of the POD_DEPARTED and DERELICT_LOADED/UNLOADED events."}, {"registry": "docs/architecture (Web Map ADR, OQ-K) and design/gdd/save-load-and-versioned-format.md", "entry": "SL-13 / SL-17 / EVENT_TRIGGERS: conditional web.state members pod_arrived_seq and berthed_seq", "change": "The Web Map ADR should name the read web.save_seq() and state that the counters are non-persisted and reset to 0 at restore. Save/Load's EVENT_TRIGGERS should poll web.save_seq() and re-read its last-seen values after a load."}]
